<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richilde, Countess of Hainaut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1031–1086</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richilde (c. 1031–1086) was Countess of Hainaut, married first to Count Hermann of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> and then, in 1051, to Baldwin VI of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>. As regent for her son Arnulf III she lost the Flemish succession war of 1071, in which Arnulf was killed at Cassel fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-i-count-of-flanders">Robert the Frisian</a>. She kept Hainaut, which passed to her son Baldwin II.</p></div>
